  "id": "COMPOUND:28935 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that N6-Acetyl-L-Lysine may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C through multiple pathways. The first path links N6-Acetyl-L-Lysine to Receptor protein-tyrosine kinase, which in turn is targeted by a complex compound that ultimately targets Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates a potential regulatory role for N6-Acetyl-L-Lysine in the signaling cascade of Receptor protein-tyrosine kinase. The second and third paths show that N6-Acetyl-L-Lysine also targets DNA polymerase nu, which is subsequently targeted by Monocillin I and Coccuvine, both of which also target Phosphodiesterase 6C. These findings suggest that N6-Acetyl-L-Lysine may act as a modulator or inhibitor of Phosphodiesterase 6C through different molecular mechanisms, possibly involving enzyme inhibition or regulatory pathways. The evidence is consistent with a role for N6-Acetyl-L-Lysine in influencing the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
